# Backend tests

Mirror `VehicleServiceTest`, `VehicleControllerTest`, `VehicleRepositoryTest` (same imports, same
naming `methodDoesWhatWhenCondition`, constants for test data, private static factory methods
`widget(...)`, `request(...)`, `response()` at the bottom).

## Mandatory matrix (one test per row – none optional)

| Class | Test | Asserts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ServiceTest | `findAllReturnsMappedWidgets` | `findAll(Sort.by("id"))` stubbed, mapped values in order |
| ServiceTest | `findByIdThrowsNotFoundWhenWidgetDoesNotExist` | `NotFoundException`, exact message `"Widget with id 99 not found"` |
| ServiceTest | `createSavesWidget` | `save` answers its argument, response fields (incl. defaults like `active=false`, normalized values) |
| ServiceTest | `createThrowsConflictWhen<Field>AlreadyExists` (each unique field) | `ConflictException` + exact message, `verify(repo, never()).save(any())` |
| ServiceTest | `create…` normalization case (only if normalized) | request `"W-001 "` → `existsByCode("w-001")` checked, stored `"w-001"` |
| ServiceTest | `updateChangesExistingWidget` | entity mutated, `verify(repo).save(entity)` |
| ServiceTest | `updateThrowsConflictWhen<Field>BelongsToAnotherWidget` | `existsBy…AndIdNot` → 409, never saves |
| ServiceTest | `updateThrowsNotFoundWhenWidgetDoesNotExist` | 404 message |
| ServiceTest | `deleteRemovesExistingWidget` / `deleteThrowsNotFoundWhenWidgetDoesNotExist` | `verify(repo).delete(entity)` / 404 |
| ControllerTest | `findAllReturnsWidgets` | 200, `$.length()`, every field incl. enum string and ISO date |
| ControllerTest | `findByIdReturnsWidget` / `findByIdReturnsNotFoundProblemWhenWidgetDoesNotExist` | 200 / 404 + `APPLICATION_PROBLEM_JSON` + `$.status` + `$.detail` |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsCreatedWidget` | 201, `header().string("Location", "http://localhost/api/widgets/1")`, `$.id` |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorsWhenRequestIsInvalid` | 400, `$.detail = "Validation failed"`, `$.errors.length()`, each `errors[i].field` **sorted alphabetically** + messages, `verifyNoInteractions(service)` |
| ControllerTest | one 400 test per custom format/constraint (e-mail, phone, checksum, …) | exact field + message |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorWhen<Enum>IsUnknown` (if enum) | `"must be one of: SMALL, LARGE"` |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsCreatedWidgetWhenOptionalFieldsAreMissing` (if optional fields) | 201 with optional fields omitted from body |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithAllRequiredFieldsWhenBodyIsEmpty` | `{}` → one error per required field, sorted |
| ControllerTest | `createTrims<Field>BeforeValidation` (if a compact constructor trims) | padded value → 201, `verify(service).create(new XRequest(..trimmed..))` |
| ControllerTest | `createReturnsConflictProblemWhen<Field>AlreadyExists` | 409 + detail |
| ControllerTest | `updateReturnsUpdatedWidget`, `updateReturnsNotFoundProblem…`, `updateReturnsBadRequestProblem…`, `updateReturnsConflictProblem…` | 200 / 404 / 400 / 409 |
| ControllerTest | `deleteReturnsNoContent` / `deleteReturnsNotFoundProblemWhenWidgetDoesNotExist` | 204 + `verify(service).delete(1L)` / 404 |
| RepositoryTest | `saveStoresWidgetThatCanBeReadBack` | save, `flush`, `clear`, `findById` → `isNotSameAs`, every field equal |
| RepositoryTest | `existsBy<Field>AndIdNotFinds<Field>OfAnotherWidget` (each unique field) | true for other row, false for itself, false for unknown value |
| RepositoryTest | `saveRejectsDuplicate<Field>` (each unique field) | `assertThatThrownBy(() -> repo.saveAndFlush(duplicate)).isInstanceOf(DataIntegrityViolationException.class)` (use `saveAndFlush` – `entityManager.flush()` throws an untranslated Hibernate exception); proves the SQL constraint exists |
| ValidatorTest (per custom constraint) | valid values, invalid values (wrong length, non-digits, separators, bad checksum), `null` → valid | plain JUnit, `@ParameterizedTest` + `@ValueSource` allowed (in `spring-boot-starter-test`), `new XValidator().isValid(value, null)` |

Nested variant adds: service 404 when parent is missing (message of the parent), 404 when the child belongs to another parent (`findByIdAndParentId` empty), list filtered by parent; controller paths with `{parentId}`, `Location` `http://localhost/api/parents/1/children/5`.

## ValidatorTest skeleton

```java
class Ean13ValidatorTest {

    private final Ean13Validator validator = new Ean13Validator();

    @ParameterizedTest
    @ValueSource(strings = {"4006381333931", "5901234123457"})
    void acceptsValidValues(String value) {
        assertThat(validator.isValid(value, null)).isTrue();
    }

    @ParameterizedTest
    @ValueSource(strings = {"", "400638133393", "40063813339310", "4006381333932", "400638133393A", "4006-381333931"})
    void rejectsInvalidValues(String value) {
        assertThat(validator.isValid(value, null)).isFalse();
    }

    @Test
    void acceptsNullBecauseRequiredIsCheckedSeparately() {
        assertThat(validator.isValid(null, null)).isTrue();
    }
}
```

## ControllerTest skeleton

```java
@WebMvcTest(WidgetController.class)
class WidgetControllerTest {

    private static final String VALID_BODY = """
            {
              "code": "w-001",
              "name": "First widget",
              "kind": "SMALL",
              "validFrom": "2026-01-15",
              "active": true
            }
            """;

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @MockitoBean
    private WidgetService widgetService;

    @Test
    void createReturnsBadRequestProblemWithFieldErrorsWhenRequestIsInvalid() throws Exception {
        String body = """
                { "code": "", "name": "%s", "kind": "SMALL" }
                """.formatted("x".repeat(51));

        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/widgets").contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON).content(body))
                .andExpect(status().isBadRequest())
                .andExpect(content().contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_PROBLEM_JSON))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.status").value(400))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.detail").value("Validation failed"))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors.length()").value(2))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors[0].field").value("code"))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors[0].message").value("must not be blank"))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors[1].field").value("name"))
                .andExpect(jsonPath("$.errors[1].message").value("size must be between 0 and 50"));
        verifyNoInteractions(widgetService);
    }
    // … rest of the matrix
}
```

Pitfalls in tests
- One field can produce two errors (e.g. `""` violates `@NotBlank` and `@Pattern`) → errors are sorted by field, then message; prefer invalid values that break exactly one rule, or assert both. Too-long e-mail: lengthen the domain with **several labels** (`"a@" + "b".repeat(50) + "." + "c".repeat(50) + ".pl"`) – a local part over 64 chars or a single domain label over 63 chars also fails `@Email`.
- Pattern rules counting digits: test the exact boundaries (phone: 8 digits invalid, 9 valid, 15 valid, 16 invalid). A value you think is invalid but is valid reaches the mocked service, which returns `null` → NPE in the controller instead of a 400.
- `@WebMvcTest` loads only the controller + advice: a service that needs a `Clock` bean is mocked, so no extra config is needed there; `@DataJpaTest` does not load services.
- Do not use `LocalDate.now()` in assertions of date rules – use a fixed `Clock` (`Clock.fixed(Instant.parse("2026-06-15T10:00:00Z"), ZoneOffset.UTC)`).
- Never edit or weaken vehicle tests to make a new slice pass.
# Frontend templates

Placeholder: `Widget` (folder `frontend/src/app/widgets/`, files `widget-*.ts`). Same fields as in
`backend.md`. Copy, rename, drop/add fields. No suffixes (`.component`, `.service`), no CSS, no
`standalone: true` (default), `templateUrl` always (no inline templates), UI text in English.

## `widget-api.ts`

```ts
import { HttpClient, httpResource } from '@angular/common/http';
import { Injectable, Signal, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

export type WidgetKind = 'SMALL' | 'LARGE';

export const WIDGET_KIND_LABELS: Record<WidgetKind, string> = {
  SMALL: 'Small',
  LARGE: 'Large',
};

export const WIDGET_KINDS = Object.keys(WIDGET_KIND_LABELS) as WidgetKind[];

export interface Widget {
  id: number;
  code: string;
  name: string;
  kind: WidgetKind;
  validFrom: string | null;
  active: boolean;
}

export type WidgetRequest = Omit<Widget, 'id'>;

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class WidgetApi {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);
  private readonly url = '/api/widgets';

  list() {
    return httpResource<Widget[]>(() => this.url, { defaultValue: [] });
  }

  get(id: Signal<number | undefined>) {
    return httpResource<Widget>(() => {
      const widgetId = id();
      return widgetId === undefined ? undefined : `${this.url}/${widgetId}`;
    });
  }

  create(request: WidgetRequest): Observable<Widget> {
    return this.http.post<Widget>(this.url, request);
  }

  update(id: number, request: WidgetRequest): Observable<Widget> {
    return this.http.put<Widget>(`${this.url}/${id}`, request);
  }

  delete(id: number): Observable<void> {
    return this.http.delete<void>(`${this.url}/${id}`);
  }
}
```

## `widget-list.ts` / `widget-list.html`

```ts
import { Component, inject, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterLink } from '@angular/router';
import { firstValueFrom } from 'rxjs';
import { loadErrorMessage, problemDetailMessage } from '../shared/problem-detail';
import { WIDGET_KIND_LABELS, Widget, WidgetApi } from './widget-api';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-widget-list',
  imports: [RouterLink],
  templateUrl: './widget-list.html',
})
export class WidgetList {
  private readonly widgetApi = inject(WidgetApi);

  protected readonly widgets = this.widgetApi.list();
  protected readonly widgetKindLabels = WIDGET_KIND_LABELS;
  protected readonly deleteError = signal<string | null>(null);

  protected loadError(error: unknown): string {
    return loadErrorMessage(error, 'Widgets not found');
  }

  protected async delete(widget: Widget): Promise<void> {
    this.deleteError.set(null);
    try {
      await firstValueFrom(this.widgetApi.delete(widget.id));
      this.widgets.reload();
    } catch (error) {
      this.deleteError.set(problemDetailMessage(error));
    }
  }
}
```

```html
<h1>Widgets</h1>

<p><a routerLink="/widgets/new">Add widget</a></p>

@if (deleteError(); as message) {
  <p class="error" role="alert">{{ message }}</p>
}

@if (widgets.isLoading()) {
  <p>Loading…</p>
} @else if (widgets.error(); as error) {
  <p class="error" role="alert">{{ loadError(error) }}</p>
} @else if (widgets.value(); as widgets) {
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Code</th>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Kind</th>
        <th>Valid from</th>
        <th>Active</th>
        <th>Actions</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      @for (widget of widgets; track widget.id) {
        <tr>
          <td>
            <a [routerLink]="['/widgets', widget.id]">{{ widget.code }}</a>
          </td>
          <td>{{ widget.name }}</td>
          <td>{{ widgetKindLabels[widget.kind] }}</td>
          <td>{{ widget.validFrom ?? '—' }}</td>
          <td>{{ widget.active ? 'Yes' : 'No' }}</td>
          <td>
            <a [routerLink]="['/widgets', widget.id, 'edit']">Edit</a>
            <button type="button" (click)="delete(widget)">Delete</button>
          </td>
        </tr>
      } @empty {
        <tr>
          <td colspan="6">No widgets yet.</td>
        </tr>
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>
}
```
`colspan` = number of columns. First column = the unique business key if the entity has one (like VIN), linked to details; otherwise the name. Person-like entities: keep natural order (first name, last name, …) and link the unique key column (e.g. e-mail) – do not reorder fields to put the key first. Detail `<h1>` = the human-readable name.

